{"author":{"id":"7be502fc1252faa17034e20337c97f83224cb75681f6f2358da33e4e8d7e55b6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794790605,"nonce":"+xoyMM+1Sda0KK3mAiF+kfgLuCE=","title":"Misleading ERROR log after a successfully served ACME HTTP-01 challenge (\"ACME challenge served, status: 500\")","message":"Hello Zentinel team,\n\nthank you for Zentinel. This is a low-priority observation about log output.\n\nObserved (tag 26.11_2, commit ea8ccf0), during a certificate renewal in the running proxy (tested against Pebble):\n\n- The challenge request is answered with HTTP 200 and the key authorization, and the CA validates it and issues the certificate.\n- At the same time the log contains ERROR lines, repeated for each request, for example:\n  `ERROR zentinel_proxy::proxy::http_trait: Proxy error occurred ... error_type=InternalError ... context: ACME challenge served error_code=500`\n  `ERROR pingora_proxy: Fail to early filter request: InternalError context: ACME challenge served, status: 500, GET /.well-known/acme-challenge/\u003ctoken\u003e`\n\nCause as far as we can tell: after writing the 200 response, early_request_filter returns `Err(Error::explain(ErrorType::InternalError, \"ACME challenge served\"))` as a signal that the request is complete (crates/proxy/src/proxy/http_trait.rs:446-473, comment \"Return error to signal request is complete\"). That error is then logged as \"Proxy error occurred\" at ERROR level (http_trait.rs:4059) and by pingora. This can look like a failing renewal and may trigger alerts.\n\nSuggestion: signal completion without an error (for example Ok(true) from the filter, if the framework allows it), or log this specific case at debug level.\n\nThank you.","files":null}]}